Thought: Test trimmed_mean over the full pool to see if including all models improves robustness.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test the best single model FT_rf, which has the lowest error overall, to see if a single model can beat the trimmed mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"FT_rf","models":["FT_rf"]}

Thought: Test a median combination on the most stable pool (pool1) to see if robust aggregation improves over best_single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a deterministic weighted average (dba) on the robust pool1 to see if it outperforms existing robust combos.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a median combination over pool2 to see if a robust non‑mean aggregator improves over the current best.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2","rationale":"robust median over moderately ranked models"}

Thought: Test a robust iterative combination (dba) on pool2 to see if exploring a different algorithm can beat the current best single model.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test best_single FT_rf restricted to pool1 to see if pool restriction changes performance.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool1","model":"FT_rf"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination over pool3 to see if median outperforms mean/trimmed_mean.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool2 using inverse_error weighting to see if it improves on the best single FT_rf.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ETS","THETA","rf","CWT_rf","DWT_rf","FT_rf"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse_error on pool3 to see if expanding the pool improves over the current leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool3","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a best_single strategy on pool2 to see if FT_rf remains best when restricted to moderately ranked models  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool2","model":"FT_rf","rationale":"check FT_rf performance on pool2"}

Thought: Test a more advanced dba on a larger pool (pool3) to see if optimization improves over the current weighted leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool3","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on pool5 using inverse_error weighting to see if it matches the current leader or improves further.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ETS","THETA","rf","CWT_rf","DWT_rf","FT_rf"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test the best single FT_rf within pool1 to see if restricting to the most stable models helps.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool1","model":"FT_rf"}

Thought: Test the best single FT_rf within the minimal pool4 (only FT_rf) to see if restricting the pool changes the score (likely same but confirm).  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","pool":"pool4","model":"FT_rf"}

Thought: Test a very simple combination on the single-model pool4 to see if a different deterministic method (median) gives any edge over the best single FT_rf.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a plain mean over pool5 to see if expanding to include ETS and THETA improves over weighted pool5.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool5","rationale":"check mean over pool5"}

